{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00311",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.31,
      "end_seconds": 7.78,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "Um, you know, sorry, doctor, I couldn't find the door at first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.88,
      "end_seconds": 12.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "That's alright, take a seat. Tell me why you've come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 14.3,
      "end_seconds": 19.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.68,
      "end_seconds": 25.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "Okay, of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.37,
      "end_seconds": 34.83,
      "duration_seconds": 8.46,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got a fever that won't go away. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.39,
      "end_seconds": 37.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.98,
      "end_seconds": 41.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "Ever since... since yesterday, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.37,
      "end_seconds": 44.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Have you found anything that eases it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.03,
      "end_seconds": 47.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Paracetamol helps a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.29,
      "end_seconds": 51.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "How often does it happen?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.18,
      "end_seconds": 58.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.94,
      "text": "It's, It's, um... not exactly... well, hard to explain, I mean—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.53,
      "end_seconds": 65.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.7,
      "text": "Let me put it another way: how many times in a typical day or week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.03,
      "end_seconds": 67.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Honestly, all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.2,
      "end_seconds": 71.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "And how severe is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.29,
      "end_seconds": 75.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Well, a five out of ten, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.73,
      "end_seconds": 85.03,
      "duration_seconds": 8.3,
      "text": "Oh, uh, and the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 85.13,
      "end_seconds": 90.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.67,
      "end_seconds": 94.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Uh, uh, I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.37,
      "end_seconds": 99.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "That's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.25,
      "end_seconds": 110.42,
      "duration_seconds": 9.17,
      "text": "As for feeling weak, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.0,
      "end_seconds": 114.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "How bad is it, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.72,
      "end_seconds": 122.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.71,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.43,
      "end_seconds": 131.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.78,
      "end_seconds": 136.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Oh, you know, about a six out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.2,
      "end_seconds": 140.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Any vomiting or blood in the stool at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.18,
      "end_seconds": 155.17,
      "duration_seconds": 13.99,
      "text": "Right, uh, no, no vomiting, no blood in the stool. I did have a dull stomach ache at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.62,
      "end_seconds": 161.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any burning when passing urine, jaundice or cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.65,
      "end_seconds": 165.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "No, um, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.86,
      "end_seconds": 169.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Right, and rash, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.4,
      "end_seconds": 172.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "No, you know, no rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 173.55,
      "end_seconds": 179.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.93,
      "text": "Right, you know, actually, doctor, I did notice rash. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.85,
      "end_seconds": 185.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.33,
      "end_seconds": 192.47,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.03,
      "end_seconds": 195.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.54,
      "end_seconds": 198.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.03,
      "end_seconds": 203.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Right, um, nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.25,
      "end_seconds": 211.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.76,
      "text": "Any long-term health problems I should know about? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.37,
      "end_seconds": 230.37,
      "duration_seconds": 19.0,
      "text": "Um, um, I have diabetes, for nearly five years. High cholesterol, for nearly five years. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know. I have heart disease. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.44,
      "end_seconds": 237.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Alright. Have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.03,
      "end_seconds": 243.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Just a stent put in my heart, two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.56,
      "end_seconds": 248.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.93,
      "end_seconds": 253.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "No, you know, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.45,
      "end_seconds": 257.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.18,
      "end_seconds": 264.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "My father had a stroke. My sister has thyroid problems."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.33,
      "end_seconds": 270.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.14,
      "end_seconds": 278.61,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "Okay, you know, so I'm on atorvastatin, 20 milligrams, maybe, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.78,
      "end_seconds": 283.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.09,
      "end_seconds": 285.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "No, it's at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.03,
      "end_seconds": 295.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.42,
      "text": "Oh, it's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a round yellow one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.78,
      "end_seconds": 297.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.64,
      "end_seconds": 310.95,
      "duration_seconds": 12.31,
      "text": "For my heart, I believe. My husband sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. Dolo. I take it 650 milligrams, when I get the fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 311.88,
      "end_seconds": 319.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the Dolo was 1300 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.19,
      "end_seconds": 322.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Alright. Did you bring the up-to-date prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.7,
      "end_seconds": 326.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.96,
      "end_seconds": 328.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Alright, any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 329.29,
      "end_seconds": 332.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "No, I don't smoke and never have."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.96,
      "end_seconds": 335.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 335.78,
      "end_seconds": 340.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.46,
      "end_seconds": 344.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.1,
      "end_seconds": 358.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Just relax your arm..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.95,
      "end_seconds": 384.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.44,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 108 over 72, saturation 98 percent, respiratory rate 16, heart rate 96, temp 38.6 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 385.06,
      "end_seconds": 386.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 389.7,
      "end_seconds": 392.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.36,
      "end_seconds": 398.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 400.95,
      "end_seconds": 402.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Breathe in deeply... and out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 415.3,
      "end_seconds": 419.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Your tummy is a bit full and tender in the lower part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 420.7,
      "end_seconds": 423.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Stay still while I have a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 431.58,
      "end_seconds": 434.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "I can't feel your liver or spleen enlarged."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 439.28,
      "end_seconds": 462.16,
      "duration_seconds": 22.88,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. So, based on the history and the examination, this looks most like typhoid fever, which we need to confirm. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. I can't rule out a viral illness yet. I'd also keep malaria in mind. I'd like to arrange a full blood count for fever. I'd like to arrange blood cultures for prolonged fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 462.61,
      "end_seconds": 464.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Alright. When can I do that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 466.24,
      "end_seconds": 469.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a malaria test for fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0072",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 470.39,
      "end_seconds": 471.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0073",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 472.73,
      "end_seconds": 500.65,
      "duration_seconds": 27.92,
      "text": "Eat only home-cooked food and drink boiled or bottled water while this is going on. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0074",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 503.51,
      "end_seconds": 504.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0075",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 506.05,
      "end_seconds": 518.62,
      "duration_seconds": 12.57,
      "text": "Please don't sit on it if the fever stays high or the tummy pain gets sharp. That's the point to get seen urgently. Come back in three days. Right, that's all I have. Is there anything you wanted to ask?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0076",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 519.52,
      "end_seconds": 523.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "I mean, no, you've explained it well. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0077",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 523.85,
      "end_seconds": 524.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}